The main issue is that bpmn.io does not automatically create a BPMN diagram from text. It is a BPMN viewer/modeler, not an AI diagram generator. If your prompt asks it to "generate BPMN from a document," you'll often end up with a blank canvas or an invalid diagram.

Instead, add the following instructions to your code-generation prompt.

Important Rendering Instructions

The generated application must produce a professional BPMN diagram with a white background similar to diagrams created in Camunda Modeler or Visio.

Appearance

- Use a pure white canvas (#FFFFFF).
- Use black text with high contrast.
- Use subtle gray borders.
- Avoid dark mode or black backgrounds.
- Use standard BPMN colors and styling.
- The diagram should look clean, simple, and professional.

Layout

- Automatically arrange all elements using a top-to-bottom layout unless left-to-right is more suitable.
- Keep equal spacing between activities.
- Align shapes perfectly.
- Never overlap shapes, text, or connectors.
- Decision gateways must be centered.
- Label outgoing paths (Yes/No or appropriate conditions).
- Keep connector routing simple with minimal crossing.
- Maintain consistent margins and padding.

BPMN Elements

Use proper BPMN elements instead of generic boxes:

- Start Event
- End Event
- User Task
- Service Task
- Manual Task
- Script Task
- Exclusive Gateway
- Parallel Gateway
- Intermediate Event
- Message Flow (where applicable)
- Sequence Flow

Automatic Improvements

If the process is too large:

- Split it into subprocesses.
- Keep each section readable.
- Avoid squeezing everything into one diagram.

Technical Requirements

- Use HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript, and jQuery if helpful.
- Use the browser version of bpmn.io via CDN (no npm).
- Generate valid BPMN 2.0 XML first, then render it using bpmn.io.
- If the BPMN XML is invalid, automatically display the validation error instead of a blank screen.
- Ensure at least one Start Event and one End Event exist.
- Ensure every task is connected by sequence flows.
- Auto-fit the diagram after loading.
- Add Zoom In, Zoom Out, Fit to Screen, and Reset View controls.

Self-Validation

Before returning the HTML, verify:

- Valid BPMN 2.0 XML.
- No blank canvas.
- No missing process objects.
- White background.
- Properly rendered BPMN elements.
- All objects connected.
- Diagram loads successfully when the HTML file is opened locally.
- No npm, build step, or additional installation required.

If the BPMN XML cannot be generated reliably from the document, stop and explain the missing information instead of generating an empty or broken diagram.One more recommendation: if your goal is simply to visualize a procedure document, Mermaid or GoJS generally produce much cleaner automatic flowcharts than bpmn.io. bpmn.io is best when you already have valid BPMN XML. For AI-generated diagrams from natural language, Mermaid or GoJS tends to be much more reliable and visually consistent.